nodecode-lowrouter is a rewrite of carboniferio's carboniferio/hermes-lowrouter-provider:

  https://github.com/carboniferio/hermes-lowrouter-provider
  commit 93a8353d495443d8157c423979ac9df2a8589db6
  Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) 2026 carboniferio (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the plugin's one payload, `lowrouter/__init__.py`, which
registers a Hermes model provider named `lowrouter` on base
https://api.lowrouter.ai/v1 with the ambient LOWROUTER_API_KEY, filters
/v1/models down to the `auto/` and `alias/` chat models that take tool calls
and fit at least 64,000 tokens of context, reads each route's context window
from the same answer (cached an hour per key and base under a hash of the
key), falls back to four named models when the catalog does not answer, and
shows the EUR credit balance from /v1/credits in /usage. In Common Lisp that
is a catalog row carrying the filtered routes (the plugin's four fallbacks
until the live catalog answers, and again whenever it does not), a credential
hook that reads LOWROUTER_API_KEY and answers a public credential without
one, a command `/lowrouter` for the balance and `/lowrouter models` for the
live list, and a section carrying the base. `plugin.yaml`, `README.md` and
the test suite around the payload were read for what the profile means, not
copied.

What was left out, and why: the `lowrouter` provider alias, the
`default_aux_model` and the per-key catalog cache have no direct
counterpart — Nodecode names a provider once, its auxiliary model is
`general.auxiliary_model`, and the worker refetches the catalog hourly
instead of caching per key. Nothing converts euros to dollars in either. The
plugin's live `/v1/models` read is the cell's own read, made with the
credential the core resolves, and the route metadata it publishes beyond the
window (price ranges, carbon estimates, candidate hosts) is left to
LowRouter's own model page.
